          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vittoria from Latin victoria, \"victory\" — a learned borrowing. EtymDB 2.1 has no row for vittoria; it derives Spanish victoria and Venetian vitoria, borrowed the same way, from victoria."
